-- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
+## Submission and Idempotency
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit with a `base_revision_id`, the system SHALL store the complete submission envelope (visit ID, base revision ID, author, idempotency key, fields, submitted_at, and server receipt time).
 - [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
-- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
-- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When an authenticated worker submits the first edit to a visit (no prior submission), the system SHALL accept a `base_revision_id` of null and assign a new revision ID.
+
+## Concurrent Edits and Revision Conflict
+
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When two or more accepted submissions name the same `base_revision_id`, the visit SHALL enter an unresolved state with `is_resolved = false` and the system SHALL list all competing revision IDs.
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a visit has no competing revisions, the system SHALL mark it `is_resolved = true` and designate the latest revision as current.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission creates a competing revision (REC-005 applies), the system SHALL NOT update the visit's current state; the current state remains the previously accepted revision until the coordinator resolves the conflict.
+
+## Retrieval
+
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return the current accepted revision's complete fields, `is_resolved` status, and the list of competing revision IDs.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a caller requests visit history, the system SHALL return all stored submission envelopes (visit ID, author, base revision ID, revision ID, submitted_at, server receipt time) in order of server receipt, and MAY omit the raw fields object.
+
+## Coordinator Resolution
+
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a coordinator submits a resolution selecting an existing competing revision, the system SHALL mark the visit `is_resolved = true`, record the coordinator's identity and timestamp, record the contributing submission IDs, and retain all original submissions.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator submits a resolution with a merged `fields` object, the system SHALL store the merged revision as a synthetic submission (author `coordinator`, parent links to the chosen competing revisions), assign a new revision ID, and mark the visit `is_resolved = true`.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a visit is resolved, the system SHALL NOT accept new submissions with `base_revision_id` pointing to any of the resolved competing revisions; new edits must cite the resolved revision's ID.
